## Helpr — Production HTTP headers
##
## Picked up by Lovable/Netlify-style hosting. Sets baseline security headers
## on every web response. Capacitor (iOS/Android) ignores these — those
## platforms get headers from WKWebView config + the meta CSP in index.html.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(self), payment=(self "https://js.stripe.com" "https://hooks.stripe.com"), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  ## CSP — script-src must keep 'unsafe-inline' for Vite-injected styles + Stripe.js, but no 'unsafe-eval' in prod.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: capacitor: ionic:; media-src 'self' blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://api.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com https://api.resend.com; frame-src https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

## Static asset cache — long TTL on hashed bundles
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

## SW + manifest must always revalidate
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw-push.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
